<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Childebert I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 496–558</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Childebert I was a Merovingian king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> from 511 to 558. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a>, he shared in the division of his father's realm, joined his brothers in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> and in murdering the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer</a>, and campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He founded the abbey later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-germain-des-pres">Saint-Germain-des-Prés</a>, and died without sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/childebert-i.jpg" alt="Childebert I" width="320" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tiers_de_sou_d'or_de_Childebert_Ier.jpg: Unknown authorUnknown author derivative work: M0tty (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiers_de_sou_d%27or_de_Childebert_Ier.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
